Z||000000||Daleford||12-12-2000||04:56 PM||||Seems to be a lot of good Canadians on this forum. Does anyone know about Canadian 5 speed transmissions in Fieros?  I am having a hard time finding a Getrag. Some people are calling theirs a Muncie? Anybody know what came in what in this country?  ||||reg||5
Z||000001||RedOktober||12-12-2000||11:34 PM||||sorry to say, but you are 2/3 there.. the other is an Isuzu unit. It all depends on the year, and motor..<P>I'm sure there are others here who could tell the difference between them...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Daleford||12-13-2000||08:32 AM||||So, does anyone know.....since Getrags are the strongest, are they only on V-6 cars? Or could one be found in a later [87-88] 4 cyl. car?<BR>How strong are Muncies in relation?   thanks<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000003||Rodney||12-13-2000||08:55 AM||||Getrags that fit the Fieros are only on the V-6. All FWD GM cars with the V-6 5 speed have the Getrag. I have heard they were also on the turbo 4's. The Quad 4 Getrag will not bolt up to the V-6 or 4. There should be no difference in "Canadian" Getrags. On my web page in the transmission section there is an articale on using the FWD Getrag in the Fiero. I now have an adapter so the internal arm design Getrag can also be used. So any FWD Getrag from a V-6 will work in a Fiero with the conversion parts. When you call a yard tell them you have a 89 Baretta. Or if you want to look for the internal arm type tell them you have a 89 Grand Prix. They will have a listing of all the Getrags that will interchange.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com" TARGET=_blank>www.rodneydickman.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Daleford||12-13-2000||09:52 AM||||Thanks Rodney. I heard of you, didn't know how to find you. I will study your site.  Still have a question, however.... When my 20 year pontiac parts veteran at the local dealer here in eastern Canada lists the standard transaxels used in all Fieros... the word Getrag never comes up! He says there are  two ..... Izuzu and Muncie! Can anyone explain?   Dale <P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Hank is Here||12-13-2000||10:07 AM||||The Getrag tranny is a German GM designed tranny, the tranny itself though was made in North America in a town name Munice somewhere, so these trannys are commonly refered to as Getrags and Muncies- one in the  same.  There is also the 4 speed which is also a Muncie but that is a creature of another animal.  This is the way I understand it to be, I could be incorrect.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Rodney||12-13-2000||11:53 AM||||Most publications call them Muncie or Muncie 5 speeds. A lot of the time you will see MG1 or MG2 which designates Getrag. Yes the Getrag word is seldom mentioned. ||||reg||1
